            "question": "Is Tampa Bay in the HVHZ?",
            "answer": "<p>No. The High-Velocity Hurricane Zone covers Miami-Dade and Broward counties only. Hillsborough, Pinellas and Pasco are coastal counties with high design wind speeds under the Florida Building Code, so the building department still reviews how the railing attaches to the deck or slab. Our engineering documents cover top-mount and side-mount spigots on concrete and on wood, with testing and blocking details, which is what the attachment review covers.</p>",
