        "t1": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "text": "<p><strong>From Bayshore Boulevard to the Pinellas beaches</strong></p><p>Tampa's waterfront starts on Bayshore Boulevard, where the sidewalk follows Hillsborough Bay past Hyde Park and Palma Ceia. It continues onto Davis Islands and Harbour Island. South Tampa neighborhoods like Beach Park, Sunset Park and Culbreath Isles have canal and bay lots with pools and docks. Downtown, the Channel District and Water Street add condo balconies over the port.</p><p>Across the Howard Frankland and Gandy bridges, St. Petersburg's Old Northeast, Snell Isle and Shore Acres sit on Tampa Bay. Clearwater and Dunedin face the Gulf side of Pinellas, and Safety Harbor sits on Old Tampa Bay. Clearwater Beach, St. Pete Beach and Treasure Island are condo territory on the barrier islands. Inland, Westchase, Carrollwood and New Tampa in Hillsborough and Wesley Chapel in Pasco are the pool-home suburbs. Hurricanes Helene and Milton in 2024 pushed surge into the low bay-front streets, and homeowners there have been repairing and raising homes since.</p>"
          }
        },
        "t2": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "text": "<p><strong>Code and permits around Tampa Bay</strong></p><p>Tampa Bay is not in the High-Velocity Hurricane Zone; that zone covers Miami-Dade and Broward only. Hillsborough, Pinellas and Pasco are coastal counties with high design wind speeds under the Florida Building Code, 8th edition (2023). Each building department reviews how a railing attaches. Tampa, Hillsborough County, St. Petersburg and Pinellas County each run their own permit office. Tampa's Architectural Review Commission also reviews exterior changes in local historic districts such as Hyde Park.</p><p>For a house, the residential code sets a 36-inch guard on a deck, balcony or landing more than 30 inches above grade. Condos need 42 inches. Pool barriers follow the Residential Swimming Pool Safety Act: at least 48 inches on the outside. Gates close on their own and open away from the pool. The 46-inch panel gives that height. See our <a href=\"/pages/florida-building-code-for-glass-railings\">Florida building code page</a>, then confirm with your building department.</p>"
          }
        },
        "t3": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "text": "<p><strong>Delivery across the bay and the DIY install</strong></p><p>Standard panels are processed in 2 to 3 business days. They arrive in 5 to 10 business days by freight carrier with a liftgate, in South Tampa, St. Petersburg or Wesley Chapel alike. The crate comes down to the driveway; for a beach condo, book the loading dock with management and tell us the address type. Custom sizes take 2 to 3 weeks in transit after processing. Orders over 3,000 dollars ship free, and the checkout price is final, with no duties, tariffs or hidden fees.</p><p>Installation is DIY with the installation guide and videos; a standard railing takes about 4 hours. Spigots fix to concrete or wood with screws sold separately, so a paver deck needs a slab or footing underneath to anchor into. Check the crate within 3 days of delivery; damage reported in that window and before installation is replaced or refunded at no cost.</p>"
          }
        }
